{
	title: 'Live ASON files',
	description: 'Provide liveFile(path, defaults, options): a plain object backed by an .ason file. Changes to the object coalesce into an atomic write (restrictive mode for secrets), external atomic replacements update the same object, and a caller can force save or close. Surface malformed files and write errors rather than silently resetting or overwriting them. Merely reading must not rewrite the file. This is the one way to keep small ASON state on disk; record that rule in tasks/README.md so nobody hand-rolls config reading and writing. Use temp dirs in tests. Lift the live-file.ts artifact and its tests, trimming what no task needs.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"The artifact contradicts the task in two places: it swallows parse errors (resets to defaults) and its test expects ASON comments to be preserved. Our ASON has no `comments` option and drops comments, so any save of a hand-edited file loses them. Don't promise otherwise.",
		'ASON parse errors quote the offending source line. For files holding secrets (auth.ason) only surface the first line of the message.',
		'The artifact\'s "own write" detection (a 100 ms flag after writing) races with the watcher. Comparing the reloaded text with the last text we wrote/read (`synced`) is reliable and needs no timer.',
		'The artifact creates a fresh proxy on every nested get, so `a.x === a.x` is false and assigning a proxy back stores a proxy in the data. Cache proxies per target and unwrap on set.',
		'Watch the directory (atomic rename swaps the inode), filter events by basename, and unref/clear the debounce timer: conventions.test.ts fails on leftover timers or watchers, and `close()` must clean both.',
		"Defaults are deep-copied through ASON; otherwise nested mutations leak into the caller's defaults object (and defaults may be proxies).",
		'An external edit wins over a local change not yet flushed; a deleted file keeps the in-memory data. Tests should override `liveFiles.onError` to capture errors instead of logging to diag.'
	],
	needs: ['8', 'p']
}
